      "text": "Given that \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\) are the roots of the polynomial \\(x^3 + 3x^2 + 4x - 11 = 0\\), we can use Vieta's formulas to find the relationships among the roots. Vieta's formulas tell us that:\n\n\\[\na + b + c = -3\n\\]\n\\[\nab + bc + ca = 4\n\\]\n\\[\nabc = 11\n\\]\n\nThe roots of the polynomial \\(x^3 + rx^2 + sx + t = 0\\) are given by \\(a+b\\), \\(b+c\\), and \\(c+a\\). We need to find the value of \\(t\\), which is the coefficient of \\(x\\) in the polynomial. According to Vieta's formulas for the new polynomial, the sum of the roots taken one at a time is equal to \\(-r\\):\n\n\\[\n(a+b) + (b+c) + (c+a) = 2(a+b+c) = 2(-3) = -6\n\\]\n\nThus, \\(r = 6\\). The product of the roots taken one at a time of the new polynomial is equal to \\(-t\\):\n\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = -t\n\\]\n\nTo find \\((a+b)(b+c)(c+a)\\), we can expand it as follows:\n\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = (a+b+c)(ab+bc+ca) - abc\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the values from Vieta's formulas:\n\n\\[\n(a+b+c)(ab+bc+ca) - abc = (-3)(4) - 11 = -12 - 11 = -23\n\\]\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = -23\n\\]\n\nSince \\((a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = -t\\), we get:\n\n\\[\n-t = -23 \\implies t = 23\n\\]\n\nThe value of \\(t\\) is \\(\\boxed{23}\\).",
