      "text": "To find the value of \\( t \\) in the equation \\( x^3 + rx^2 + sx + t = 0 \\) given that the roots are \\( a+b \\), \\( b+c \\), and \\( c+a \\), we can use Vieta's formulas. According to Vieta's formulas, for a cubic equation \\( x^3 + px^2 + qx + r = 0 \\) with roots \\( p, q, r \\), we have:\n\n\\[\np + q + r = -p\n\\]\n\n\\[\npq + qr + rp = q\n\\]\n\n\\[\npqr = -r\n\\]\n\nHere, the roots of the equation \\( x^3 + 3x^2 + 4x - 11 = 0 \\) are \\( a, b, c \\). So, we have:\n\n\\[\na + b + c = -3\n\\]\n\n\\[\nab + bc + ca = 4\n\\]\n\n\\[\nabc = 11\n\\]\n\nThe roots of the equation \\( x^3 + rx^2 + sx + t = 0 \\) are \\( a+b \\), \\( b+c \\), and \\( c+a \\). According to Vieta's formulas for this equation, the sum of the roots is:\n\n\\[\n(a+b) + (b+c) + (c+a) = 2(a + b + c) = 2(-3) = -6\n\\]\n\nSince the sum of the roots of \\( x^3 + rx^2 + sx + t = 0 \\) is \\( -r \\), we have \\( r = 6 \\).\n\nNext, we need to find the sum of the product of the roots taken two at a time:\n\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c) + (b+c)(c+a) + (c+a)(a+b)\n\\]\n\nExpanding each term, we get:\n\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c) = ab + ac + b^2 + bc\n\\]\n\n\\[\n(b+c)(c+a) = bc + ba + c^2 + ca\n\\]\n\n\\[\n(c+a)(a+b) = ca + cb + a^2 + ab\n\\]\n\nAdding these together, we get:\n\n\\[\n(ab + ac + b^2 + bc) + (bc + ba + c^2 + ca) + (ca + cb + a^2 + ab) = 2(ab + ac + bc + ba + ca + cb) = 2(ab + bc + ca) = 2 \\cdot 4 = 8\n\\]\n\nSo, \\( s = 8 \\).\n\nFinally, the product of the roots is:\n\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c)(c+a)\n\\]\n\nExpanding this, we get:\n\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = (a+b)(bc + c^2 + ab + ac) = (a+b)(ab + ac + bc + c^2) = a^2b + a^2c + ab^2 + abc + abc + b^2c + abc + b^2a + ac^2 = a^2b + a^2c + b^2c + b^2a + c^2a + c^2b + 3abc\n\\]\n\nSince \\( abc = 11 \\), we have:\n\n\\[\na^2b + a^2c + b^2c + b^2a + c^2a + c^2b + 3 \\cdot 11 = a^2b + a^2c + b^2c + b^2a + c^2a + c^2b + 33\n\\]\n\nWe already know that \\( ab + bc + ca = 4 \\), so:\n\n\\[\na^2b + a^2c + b^2c + b^2a + c^2a + c^2b + 33 = 8(4) + 33 = 32 + 33 = 65\n\\]\n\nTherefore, \\( t = -65 \\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-65}\n\\]",
