      "text": "To find the value of \\( t \\) in the equation \\( x^3 + rx^2 + sx + t = 0 \\) where the roots are \\( a+b \\), \\( b+c \\), and \\( c+a \\), we will use Vieta's formulas. Let's start by analyzing the given polynomial \\( x^3 + 3x^2 + 4x - 11 = 0 \\), whose roots are \\( a \\), \\( b \\), and \\( c \\).\n\nBy Vieta's formulas, for the polynomial \\( x^3 + 3x^2 + 4x - 11 = 0 \\), we have:\n\\[\na + b + c = -3,\n\\]\n\\[\nab + bc + ca = 4,\n\\]\n\\[\nabc = 11.\n\\]\n\nNext, we consider the polynomial \\( x^3 + rx^2 + sx + t = 0 \\) with roots \\( a+b \\), \\( b+c \\), and \\( c+a \\). Using Vieta's formulas again, we need to find the sums and products of these roots.\n\nFirst, the sum of the roots:\n\\[\n(a+b) + (b+c) + (c+a) = 2(a + b + c).\n\\]\nSince \\( a + b + c = -3 \\), we have:\n\\[\n2(a + b + c) = 2(-3) = -6.\n\\]\nSo, the coefficient \\( r \\) of \\( x^2 \\) is \\( -6 \\).\n\nNext, the sum of the product of the roots taken two at a time:\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c) + (b+c)(c+a) + (c+a)(a+b).\n\\]\nExpanding each term, we get:\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c) = ab + ac + b^2 + bc,\n\\]\n\\[\n(b+c)(c+a) = bc + ba + c^2 + ca,\n\\]\n\\[\n(c+a)(a+b) = ca + ab + a^2 + b^2.\n\\]\nAdding these, we have:\n\\[\nab + ac + b^2 + bc + bc + ba + c^2 + ca + a^2 + b^2 = 2(ab + ac + bc) + a^2 + b^2 + c^2.\n\\]\nWe know from the identity \\( a^2 + b^2 + c^2 = (a+b+c)^2 - 2(ab + bc + ca) \\) that:\n\\[\na^2 + b^2 + c^2 = (-3)^2 - 2 \\cdot 4 = 9 - 8 = 1.\n\\]\nThus, the sum of the product of the roots taken two at a time is:\n\\[\n2(ab + ac + bc) + 1.\n\\]\nFrom Vieta's formulas for the polynomial \\( x^3 + 3x^2 + 4x - 11 = 0 \\), we have \\( ab + bc + ca = 4 \\). Therefore:\n\\[\n2 \\cdot 4 + 1 = 8 + 1 = 9.\n\\]\nSo, the coefficient \\( s \\) of \\( x \\) is \\( 9 \\).\n\nFinally, the product of the roots:\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = abc + ab(a+b) + bc(b+c) + ca(c+a) + a(b+c) + b(c+a) + c(a+b).\n\\]\nExpanding each term, we get:\n\\[\nabc + ab(a+b) + bc(b+c) + ca(c+a) + a(b+c) + b(c+a) + c(a+b).\n\\]\nThis can be simplified using the identity:\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = a^2b + ab^2 + b^2c + bc^2 + c^2a + ca^2 + 3abc + a^2b + b^2c + bc^2 + ca^2 + a^2c + b^2a + c^2a + ac^2.\n\\]\nAfter simplification, we find:\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = a^2b + ab^2 + b^2c + bc^2 + c^2a + ca^2 + 3abc + 3a^2b + 3ab^2 + 3b^2c + 3bc^2.\n\\]\nGrouping the terms, we get:\n\\[\na^2b + ab^2 + b^2c + bc^2 + c^2a + ca^2 + 4abc = abc(a+b+c) + 3ab(a+b) + 3bc(b+c) + 3ca(c+a).\n\\]\nUsing \\( a+b+c = -3 \\) and the products \\( ab + bc + ca = 4 \\):\n\\[\nabc(a+b+c) + 3ab(a+b) + 3bc(b+c) + 3ca(c+a) = 11(-3) + 3 \\cdot 4(-3) + 3 \\cdot 4(-3) + 3 \\cdot 4(-3) = -33 - 36 - 36 - 36 = -151.\n\\]\nSo, the product of the roots \\( t \\) is \\( -151 \\).\n\nThus, the value of \\( t \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-151}.\n\\]",
